     "heading": "13. Text-to-speech, speech recognition, and voice features",
-    "body": "The App uses your device's built-in text-to-speech engine through expo-speech to pronounce English phrases and example sentences. Based on the current implementation, this pronunciation is generated on device and Knowly does not receive the generated text-to-speech audio. Some approved Community Packs also include pre-generated audio for their cards, created on our servers from the card text by our AI provider's text-to-speech service, as described in the Community Packs section; it does not use your voice or anything you type.\n\nWhere speech recognition, pronunciation practice, or voice dialogue features are enabled, the App may request microphone and speech recognition permissions. Depending on the feature, speech may be processed on device or by platform speech services, and a transcript or recognized text may be used by the App. If you use an AI voice dialogue feature, the transcript or recognized text may be sent to the AI provider as described in the AI features section. Do not say sensitive personal, confidential, payment, medical, legal, financial, or emergency information in voice features.\n\nSome of the libraries that power these voice features are general-purpose media and animation libraries that also support video capture and motion sensors. Because of this, on some platforms the operating system may list camera or motion permissions for the App. The App does not take photos, record video, open the camera, or read motion and fitness sensors, and it never asks you for those permissions; the only sensor input the App captures is microphone audio for the voice features described above."
+    "body": "The App uses your device's built-in text-to-speech engine through expo-speech to pronounce English phrases and example sentences. Based on the current implementation, this pronunciation is generated on device and Knowly does not receive the generated text-to-speech audio. Some approved Community Packs also include pre-generated audio for their cards, created on our servers from the card text by our AI provider's text-to-speech service, as described in the Community Packs section; it does not use your voice or anything you type.\n\nWhere speech recognition, pronunciation practice, or voice dialogue features are enabled, the App may request microphone and speech recognition permissions. Depending on the feature, speech may be processed on device or by platform speech services, and a transcript or recognized text may be used by the App. If you use an AI voice dialogue feature, the transcript or recognized text may be sent to the AI provider as described in the AI features section. Do not say sensitive personal, confidential, payment, medical, legal, financial, or emergency information in voice features.\n\nIn AI dialogues, when you answer by voice, the recording is kept only in the App's temporary storage on your device so that you can play your own message back, and it is removed when it is no longer needed; Knowly does not receive the recording. Only the recognised text of your answer is sent, as described in the AI features section. On Android, speech recognition uses your device's system speech recognizer, which may be provided by Google and may process your voice under its own terms.\n\nSome of the libraries that power these voice features are general-purpose media and animation libraries that also support video capture and motion sensors. Because of this, on some platforms the operating system may list camera or motion permissions for the App. The App does not take photos, record video, open the camera, or read motion and fitness sensors, and it never asks you for those permissions; the only sensor input the App captures is microphone audio for the voice features described above."
   },
